-- Forty interview questions about band dynamics, media scandals, merch and club culture.
WITH seed(category,media_types,question_text,a,b,c,d) AS (VALUES
('band_management',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'How do you welcome a new musician into an established band?','We make space for their ideas and help them feel included.','Clear expectations make the transition easier for everyone.','A new player should be encouraged to challenge old habits.','First we teach them where the rehearsal room light switch is.'),
('band_management',ARRAY['radio','tv','podcast']::text[],'Would you ever let a substitute musician play your biggest show?','If they respect the songs and the band, yes.','We''d rehearse thoroughly and plan for the change.','An unexpected player might bring new life to the performance.','As long as they know which end of the guitar to hold.'),
('band_management',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'What should happen if bandmates disagree over a major recording expense?','Everyone should be able to explain their concerns honestly.','We''d review the budget and decide together.','If an idea really matters, I''d fight for it with evidence.','I definitely shouldn''t be given the company credit card.'),
('band_management',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'How do you handle an invitation to join another band temporarily?','I''d be open to collaboration if it respects my commitments.','I''d check schedules and discuss it with the current band first.','Playing with different musicians can make us all better.','My band insists I return with all my guitar pedals.'),
('band_management',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Can a band''s leader make every decision without losing trust?','A leader has to listen to the people doing the work.','We share responsibilities and explain important decisions.','Strong leadership means taking risks and owning mistakes.','Being leader doesn''t mean choosing everyone''s sandwich.'),
('band_management',ARRAY['radio','tv','podcast']::text[],'What would you do if a bandmate completely forgot their part on stage?','I''d help them recover and keep the song moving.','We have signals and arrangements for unexpected mistakes.','A good band turns a disaster into a memorable moment.','I''d just sing the guitar riff until they remember.'),
('band_management',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'When should a band replace a member who keeps missing rehearsals?','I''d talk with them first and find out what''s happening.','Consistent expectations and fair warnings are important.','Nobody should hold everyone else back indefinitely.','I''ll give them an alarm clock before I give them a final warning.'),
('band_management',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'What makes a band disagreement productive instead of destructive?','Focusing on the music rather than attacking each other.','Everyone gets heard before we settle on a direction.','I''d rather have an honest argument than silent resentment.','We ban personal insults and arguments over takeaway orders.'),
('band_management',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Should every band member have a chance to speak in interviews?','Yes, everyone has their own experience of the music.','We rotate appearances based on interest and availability.','Fans deserve to hear from the musicians behind every part.','Only after the drummer promises not to reveal our nicknames.'),
('band_management',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'What would convince you to reunite with a former bandmate?','Honest conversations and a shared reason to make music again.','I''d need to know the old problems had genuinely changed.','A reunion should create something new, not just nostalgia.','They''d have to return the amplifier they borrowed.'),
('media_scandal',ARRAY['tv','podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'What would you do if a gossip site invented a backstage argument?','We''d correct the record without attacking anyone.','We''d save evidence and ask for a factual correction.','I''d call out the invented story rather than feed it.','I''d invite them to our next incredibly boring soundcheck.'),
('media_scandal',ARRAY['tv','podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Should artists respond immediately when a rumour starts trending?','I think it''s better to understand the facts first.','We''d agree on a measured response with the people affected.','Waiting can be worse if a damaging lie spreads quickly.','I''d turn off notifications before typing anything foolish.'),
('media_scandal',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'How would you react if an old private message was shared publicly?','I''d be honest about the context without exposing others.','We''d check authenticity and protect anyone''s private details.','If it''s genuine and harmful, I''d take responsibility directly.','I hope nobody finds the embarrassing band-name suggestions.'),
('media_scandal',ARRAY['tv','radio','podcast']::text[],'Is controversy ever useful when you''re promoting new music?','Attention only helps if the music has something worth hearing.','I''d rather let performance and real conversations build interest.','An uncomfortable truth can generate an important debate.','If the scandal is my haircut, I''ll survive.'),
('media_scandal',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Would you apologise publicly for something a bandmate said?','I''d support them in taking responsibility where appropriate.','The person involved should be heard before we make a statement.','I won''t defend something harmful just to protect our image.','I''ll apologise for my own awful jokes first.'),
('media_scandal',ARRAY['tv','podcast','magazine']::text[],'What if an interviewer keeps asking about a false accusation?','I''d explain the facts once and move back to the music.','We''d offer reliable information and set clear boundaries.','I''d challenge the premise rather than repeat the rumour.','If they want fiction, I''ll recommend our album artwork.'),
('media_scandal',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Would you cancel an endorsement because a brand becomes controversial?','If its actions conflict with our values, I''d reconsider it.','We''d review the facts and terms before making a decision.','I''d walk away from a deal that betrayed our fans'' trust.','The promotional posters can become practice-room wallpaper.'),
('media_scandal',ARRAY['tv','radio','podcast']::text[],'Should musicians ever use a public feud to settle private disagreements?','Private problems deserve private conversations where possible.','We''d try mediation before posting competing statements.','A public challenge is tempting but rarely solves anything.','We''ve agreed not to argue about bass levels online.'),
('media_scandal',ARRAY['magazine','newspaper','podcast']::text[],'When is it appropriate to issue a formal correction to the press?','When a material fact is wrong and the truth matters.','I''d point to the exact error and provide verifiable details.','A correction is better than letting a false story become history.','Please correct the venue name before the fans go to the wrong city.'),
('media_scandal',ARRAY['tv','podcast','magazine']::text[],'What would you say to fans disappointed by your behaviour?','I''d listen, own what I did wrong and try to improve.','Real accountability means action, not just a polished statement.','You can disagree with me, and I''ll still respect you.','I can''t promise perfection, only fewer disastrous posts.'),
('merch_design',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','internet']::text[],'Would you wear a fan-designed item on stage?','If it captured the spirit of the band, I''d love to.','We''d arrange permission and credit the designer properly.','A daring fan creation could become our signature look.','I draw the line at a hat taller than the microphone.'),
('merch_design',ARRAY['radio','tv','podcast']::text[],'What makes a piece of band merchandise worth owning?','It should be useful, well made and connected to the music.','Good design and reasonable pricing matter.','A truly original item can become a little piece of music history.','A shirt that survives the washing machine is a great start.'),
('merch_design',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Would you rather sell affordable shirts or limited premium jackets?','I''d want something accessible for every fan.','We can offer different options without making anyone feel excluded.','An ambitious design is worth making if quality is exceptional.','If the jacket costs more than a guitar, maybe not.'),
('merch_design',ARRAY['tv','podcast','magazine']::text[],'How important are costumes and outfits to a stage persona?','Clothing can help express the feeling of a song.','I choose outfits that look right and let me perform comfortably.','The right silhouette can define a whole live era.','I just need pockets that can hold a guitar pick.'),
('merch_design',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Should venues allow local artists to sell their own designs at gigs?','Yes, it gives creative people a valuable audience.','We''d want clear agreements and fair stall fees.','A concert should support the wider local creative scene.','Make room for the artist who paints our ridiculous tour posters.'),
('merch_design',ARRAY['radio','tv','podcast']::text[],'Would you play a show in an extravagant custom-made outfit?','Absolutely, if it helps tell the story of the performance.','The design has to be safe and practical under stage lights.','Give me something theatrical enough to stop a crowd talking.','As long as I can still reach the guitar strings.'),
('merch_design',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'What would persuade you to make a seasonal limited-edition merch design?','A creative idea that genuinely fits the band''s music.','We''d check production lead times and avoid waste.','A wild seasonal design could become a fan favourite.','I''ll approve it if nobody puts a pumpkin over my eyes.'),
('merch_design',ARRAY['internet','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Would you include player-style character art on band posters and merchandise?','Personal portraits could make each design feel more connected.','We''d use consistent artwork and obtain everyone''s approval.','I''d turn the whole band into an unforgettable illustrated lineup.','Please make my cartoon version look taller.'),
('merch_design',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'How would you respond to complaints about poor-quality band merchandise?','I''d take them seriously and put things right for fans.','We''d review suppliers and improve checks before selling more.','A bad product with our name on it damages everyone''s trust.','If the logo peels off after one wash, that''s our problem.'),
('merch_design',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Would you sell a collectible instrument made in your own workshop?','It could be a wonderful way to share a part of our craft.','Only after checking the instrument''s quality and support.','A unique hand-built guitar could become a legendary fan item.','I''d rather it be played than kept next to a dusty trophy.'),
('nightclub_culture',ARRAY['radio','podcast','tv']::text[],'Could a nightclub residency teach a musician new performance skills?','Absolutely, working a room regularly sharpens your instincts.','It would help us learn pacing, mixing and reading an audience.','I''d use a residency to try ideas too daring for the main stage.','I''d finally learn how the DJ keeps the cables untangled.'),
('nightclub_culture',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'What makes a club night feel different from every other venue in town?','A distinctive musical identity and a welcoming community.','Good staff, sound and programming build a loyal audience.','One fearless resident DJ can define an entire scene.','I appreciate a place where the coat check actually works.'),
('nightclub_culture',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Would you combine live guitar with a DJ''s electronic set?','Yes, it could create something energetic and unexpected.','We''d rehearse transitions carefully so both elements work.','I''d improvise over the mix and see where the room takes us.','As long as I don''t accidentally unplug the decks.'),
('nightclub_culture',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Should a nightclub invest first in sound equipment or decorative lighting?','Great sound is the foundation of a memorable night.','I''d budget for safe, reliable production overall.','I''d rather have an incredible mix in a plain room.','Nobody can dance to a broken speaker, however pretty the lasers.'),
('nightclub_culture',ARRAY['radio','tv','podcast']::text[],'How can a DJ recover after making an awkward transition live?','Stay calm, find the beat and rebuild the groove.','Preparation gives you several tracks that can recover the room.','A mistake can become an unexpected creative turn.','I smile like that scratch was completely deliberate.'),
('nightclub_culture',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'What makes a nightclub a good space for emerging artists?','An inclusive crowd and real opportunities to perform.','Fair pay, safe equipment and good feedback all matter.','Give newcomers a genuine chance at prime-time slots.','And don''t put the rookie on a deck with a missing knob.'),
('nightclub_culture',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Would you rather DJ to a packed dancefloor or an intimate listening room?','An engaged crowd matters more than the number of people.','Each setting requires a different journey through the music.','I''d love the challenge of turning a tiny room into a frenzy.','Fewer people means fewer witnesses to my bad dancing.'),
('nightclub_culture',ARRAY['radio','podcast','tv']::text[],'What makes a great closing track for a club night?','It should leave people with a lasting feeling.','I''d build toward a satisfying ending without rushing it.','The final track should make everyone want one more hour.','Something that tells them the lights really are coming on.'),
('nightclub_culture',ARRAY['podcast','magazine','newspaper']::text[],'Should nightclub owners let residents shape the weekly music programme?','Yes, residents understand the people who come back every week.','I''d balance their expertise with the venue''s wider goals.','Giving creative freedom to the right DJ can transform a place.','Let them choose the songs, not the colour of the fire exits.'),
('nightclub_culture',ARRAY['radio','podcast','magazine']::text[],'Would you play an unannounced underground set under a different name?','Yes, it would be refreshing to let the music speak first.','I''d make sure the organiser and venue could support it properly.','I''d love to surprise a room with something completely different.','My disguise would last until I reached for the guitar.')
), inserted AS (
INSERT INTO public.interview_questions
(category,media_types,question_text,option_a_text,option_a_effects,option_b_text,option_b_effects,option_c_text,option_c_effects,option_d_text,option_d_effects)
SELECT s.category,s.media_types,s.question_text,
s.a,jsonb_build_object('fame_mult',1.03,'fan_mult',1.04,'cash_mult',1.00,'reputation',jsonb_build_object('authentic',2,'professional',1)),
s.b,jsonb_build_object('fame_mult',1.01,'fan_mult',1.02,'cash_mult',1.02,'reputation',jsonb_build_object('diplomatic',2,'professional',2)),
s.c,jsonb_build_object('fame_mult',1.05,'fan_mult',0.99,'cash_mult',0.99,'reputation',jsonb_build_object('bold',2,'rebellious',2)),
s.d,jsonb_build_object('fame_mult',1.02,'fan_mult',1.01,'cash_mult',1.00,'reputation',jsonb_build_object('unpredictable',2,'authentic',1))
FROM seed s WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.interview_questions q WHERE lower(btrim(q.question_text))=lower(btrim(s.question_text)))
RETURNING id
) SELECT count(*)::integer AS inserted_count FROM inserted;